# Desktop only

Krayon is built for desktop. Do not design, build, or fix layouts for phones or narrow viewports.

The supported width is **1200px and wider**. Every screen must render properly at 1200px and keep working as the window gets wider. Below 1200px is out of scope.

## When changing UI

- Build the desktop layout as the default, not a phone layout that expands later.
- At 1200px, columns, side panels, toolbars, and the lesson player must be visible and usable. No clipped text, overlapping controls, or horizontal page scroll.
- Wider than 1200px, content may grow or stay in a max width. It must not break, overlap, or leave a broken gap.
- Do not add phone navigation, bottom sheets, hamburger menus, or touch-only targets.
- Do not spend time on `sm:` / `md:` stacking. Existing small-screen classes can stay; do not add more to chase a phone layout.

```tsx
// Bad: the real layout only appears above 1280px, so 1200px is still a phone stack
<main className="grid xl:grid-cols-[260px_1fr]">

// Good: desktop columns are in place by 1200px
<main className="grid min-[1200px]:grid-cols-[260px_minmax(0,1fr)]">
```
